  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing a Systemic Approach to Diaspora Engagement for Ukraine&#x2019;s Resilience, &amp; Economic Recovery</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine has a very large and successful diaspora community living throughout Europe and North America whp, for decades, have been contributing to humanitarian and development support in Ukraine. However, diaspora efforts have not been well coordinated with government development initiatives and thus, have tended to be sporadic and limited in their contributions to more systemic and sustainavle development. This project aims to lay the groundwork for more systematized cooperation within the various areas of common interest and action between diaspora groups and government initiatives, as well as broader IOM and UN programming in Ukraine and as part of te Ukraine response. Specifically, the project will look to assess cooperation possibilities in three fields of diaspora engagement: (i) humanitarian response; (ii) social development (including psycho-social support) and; (iii) economic development.</narrative>
  </description>
